  "longBusinessSummary": "BREMER LAGERHAUS-GESELLSCHAFT -Aktiengesellschaft von 1877- provides logistics and supply chain management services worldwide. It operates through Automobile, Contract, and Container segments. The company offers seaport terminals for car handling, as well as inland terminals; vehicle storage, technical services, and multimodal distribution services by road, rail, and inland waterways; distributes vehicles to car dealers; and provides ancillary services, such as customs clearance and export and import administration. It also provides procurement, production, distribution logistics, and reverse and spare parts logistics; consolidate, process, pack, and ship goods for the supply of production plants; complex system services; supply and disposal of waste removal from production lines, on-site logistics, reverse logistics management, and complex assemblies; and handle and store refrigerated and frozen good, and related services. In addition, the company offers container handling services; intermodal services comprising transport of sea containers to and from the terminals, repairs, depot storage and trading of containers, cargo-modal, and technical services; and freight forwarding services. The company was incorporated in 1877 and is headquartered in Bremen, Germany.",
